      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "With the new dynamic world rows, it should be possible to integrate a option for users to customize this on their end.\n\nThis would make good use of the website and giving the users the ability to make it how they see fit.\nIt also adds the possibility for custom rows with our own query parameters.\n\nWith this we could:\n - Hide Rows\n - Reorder\n - Have custom parameters\n \nSome world rows should be prevented from hiding, but still allow reorder.\n\nAll main rows will be available in a active/inactive setting. \nSo if you got on the website, you'll be able to see any new or existing rows that isn't active in your own set up. Then add the ones you want.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-10-30T21:08:52.364Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "e.g. I would like to have my own avatars above my favorite, and my favorite worlds above every other world in the menu. Allowing users to sort the rows would be pretty useful for a faster menu navigation. I very rarely use the worlds menu, since I most often hang around friends and when I do use the world menu, then to look into my newly uploaded world and test it.",
